        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "Solve the irrational inequality \\(\\sqrt{x+4}-\\sqrt{x-1}\\ge 1\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The domain is \\(x\\ge1\\). Rationalising gives \\(\\sqrt{x+4}-\\sqrt{x-1}=\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{x+4}+\\sqrt{x-1}}\\). Thus the inequality is equivalent to \\(\\sqrt{x+4}+\\sqrt{x-1}\\le5\\), whose equality occurs at \\(x=5\\). Therefore, the solution set is \\([1,5]\\).",
