        "question_title": "Solve \\(\\sqrt{x^2-5x+6}\\le x-2\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Since the left side is nonnegative, \\(x-2\\ge0\\). The radicand condition gives \\(x\\le2\\) or \\(x\\ge3\\). Thus the possible values are \\(x=2\\) or \\(x\\ge3\\). Squaring for \\(x\\ge3\\) yields \\((x-2)(x-3)\\le(x-2)^2\\), which is always true. Hence the solution is \\(\\{2\\}\\cup[3,\\infty)\\).",
